g Pil (Kim Jaejoong) and Kang Soo Jin (UEE) attended this school.'),(5004489,'<Manhole - Wonderland Pill(맨홀-이상한 나라의 필)>The scene where Bong Pil (Kim Jaejoong) and Kang Soo Jin (Uee) sit in front of this mural in episode 7 of Manhole - Wonderland (KBS2, 2017)'),(5004490,'<Manhole-Strange Country\'s Pill(맨홀-이상한 나라의 필)>In episode 7, Bong Pil (Kim Jaejoong) and Gang Soojin (Uee) sit in front of this mural. She confesses her love. However, before he can tell her that he loves her, he disappears, leaving her heartbroken.'),(5004491,'<Manhole - Alice in Wonderland\'s Phil(맨홀-이상한 나라의 필)>The scene where Bong-pil (Kim Jae-joong) is possessed by Jo Seok-tae (B1A4 Baro) while falling asleep.'),(5004492,'<View from afar with blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 1, Yeo-jun (Park Ji-hoon) suggests to So-bin (Kang Min-ah) to do bungee jumping together.'),(5004493,'<Seen as green in spring from afar(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 7, Nam Soo-hyun (played by Bae In-hyuk) distributes flyers in front of exit 3 of this station and also does another part-time job.'),(5004494,'<From a distance, it looks like a blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)> In episode 3, Yeojun (Park Jihoon) brought Kim Sobi (Kang Mina) to this shopping mall.'),(5004495,'<View of blue spring from afar(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>Take the subway to this station and head towards the university from Exit 4.'),(5004496,'<Seen from afar, a green spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episodes 2 and 3, Yeo-jun (Park Ji-hoon) arrives at the entrance of this residential complex that leads to his parents\' house together with his brother Yeo-jun-wan (Nainwoo).'),(5004497,'<from afar, it looks like a blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>After breaking up with Kim Sobin (Kang Min-a) in episode 4, Yeo Jun (Park Ji-hoon) receives a call from a friend and attends a party at this bar.'),(5004498,'<From afar, it looks like a blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 3, Yeojoon (Park Jihoon) and his brother Yeojunwan (Na Inwoo) cross this bridge to visit their parents and come back.'),(5004500,'<Distant view of blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 1, Nam Soo-hyun (played by Bae In-hyuk) appears in a scene where he is working part-time in front of this intersection.'),(5004501,'<From a distance, it looks like a blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>Freshmen from Myungil University\'s Department of Business Administration have their MT at the campground.'),(5004502,'<Far view in blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 2, Yeo-jun comes to pick up his brother Yeo-junwan (Nine Woo) in front of this place where a scene of parents waiting is shown.'),(5004503,'<Seen from afar, it looks like a lively spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In the drama, the protagonist Yeojoon (Park Jihoon) is a student at \'Myungil University\'.'),(5004504,'<From far away it looks like a blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 10, Kim Sobin (Kang Min-a) meets her mother (Jung Seo-yeon) at this cafe.'),(5004505,'<Seen from afar, a blue spring(멀리서 보면 푸른 봄)>In episode 3 of \'Seen from Afar, a Blue Spring\' (KBS2, 2021), Yeojun (played by Park Ji-hoon) appears bringing Kim Sobin (played by Kang Min-ah) to this shopping mall.'),(5004506,'<Stop Moment: About Time(멈추고 싶은 순간: 어바웃 타임)>In episode 10, Choi Michaela (Lee Sung Kyung) calls Park Jae-kwang (Kim Hae Sook) and asks if he is okay, who was taken to the emergency room.'),(5004507,'<Moment of Stop: About Time(멈추고 싶은 순간: 어바웃 타임)>In episode 9, Bae Soo-bong (played by Im Se-mi) calls Kim Joon-ah (played by Kim Gyoo-ri) and Choi Mi-kae-la (played by Lee Sung-kyung) to have brunch together. Here, Soo-bong is amazed to see past (Joon-ah), present (Mi-kae-la), and future (her) all meeting face to face. She expresses that because she and Doha are going to get married soon, it is better for him to resolve things in the past before marrying her and finish things in the present.'),(5004508,'<The Moment of Stop: About Time(멈추고 싶은 순간: 어바웃 타임)>In episode 9, Bae Soo-bong (played by Im Se-mi) is shown calling Kim Joon and Choi Mi-ka (played by Lee Sung-kyung). Ah (played by Kim Gyu-ri) goes to t