.'),(5004556,'<Melancholia(멜랑꼴리아)>In episode 1, Ji Yoon-soo (played by Im Soo-jung) and Baek Seung-yoo (played by Lee Do-hyun) agree to meet outside this building (also known as \'Hangok Art Hall\') to exchange bags.'),(5004557,'<Melangcollia(멜랑꼴리아)>Baek Seung-yoo (played by Lee Do-hyun) participates in a talk related to winning the 2021 Lucifer Award in the seventh episode. During the Q&A session, he receives a question from someone with the nickname \'Calculous\', and he mistakenly thinks of her as Ji Yoon-soo (played by Im Soo-jung).'),(5004558,'<Melangcollia(멜랑꼴리아)>It appears as the way to his apartment when Ji Yoon-su takes Baek Seung-yu (Lee Do-hyun) home in episode 12.'),(5004559,'<Mellangcollia(멜랑꼴리아)>A gathering of the mothers of students at Aseong High School was held here to celebrate the birthday of Noh Jung-ah (Jin Kyung) in Episode 1.'),(5004560,'<Mellangcollia(멜랑꼴리아)>In episode 4, Ji Yoon-soo (played by Lim Soo-jung) and Baek Seung-yoo (played by Lee Do-hyun) visit this gallery on a day trip to Jeju. Note: Only the exterior of the gallery is displayed, and it appears that this exhibition took place at Bunker de Lumieres.'),(5004561,'<Melancholia(멜랑꼴리아)>In episode 4, Ji Yoon-soo (Im Soo-jung) and Baek Seung-yoo (Lee Dohyun) check in at this airport to board a flight to Jeju.'),(5004562,'<Melancholia(멜랑꼴리아)>This gallery appears in the drama \'The Third Charm\' when Ji Yoon Soo (played by Im Soo Jung) and Baek Seung Yu (played by Lee Do Hyun) visit to see the \'Star\' exhibition.'),(5004563,'<Melancholia(멜랑꼴리아)>Main characters including Ji Yoon-soo (played by Lim Soo-jung), Baek Seung-yoo (played by Lee Do-hyun), and Sung Ye-rin (played by Woo Da-bi) work as math teachers at \'Asung High School\'. In episode 1, Ji Yoon-soo (Lim Soo-jung) finds Baek Seung-yoo (Lee Do-hyun) sleeping in a barn next to an art museum after searching for him who had solved difficult exam problems anonymously.'),(5004564,'<Melancholia(멜랑꼴리아)>In episode 7, Baek Seung-yoo (Lee Do-hyun) comes to this elderly man\'s house to find a professor and meets Ji Yoon-soo (Im Soo-jung) for the first time.'),(5004565,'<Melancholia(멜로가 체질)>Director Lee Eun-jung (Jeon Yeobin) films a documentary depicting the everyday life of actress Lee Somin (Lee Jubin). In episode 6, the actress visits a sledding rink to spend time before getting busy with work.'),(5004566,'<Melting Me Softly(멜로가 체질)>In episode 8, Hwang Han Joo (Han Ji Eun) and drama production company CEO Lee So Jin (Kim Young Ah) finish their dinner with rookie playwright Im Jin Joo (Chun Woo Hee) and director Son Beom Soo (Ahn Jae Hong) and have drinks at this place.'),(5004567,'<Meloga physique(멜로가 체질)>Frequent Japanese restaurant of author Jung Hye-jung and JBC director'),(5004568,'<Melo is My Nature(멜로가 체질)>The restaurant where Cheon Woo-hee left and Lee Yoo-jin dined alone.'),(5004569,'<Melting Pot(멜로가 체질)>Restaurant where Cheon Woo-hee and Han Ji-eun ate steak'),(5004570,'<Melting Me Softly(멜로가 체질)>In episode 12, Jinju (Chun Woo-hee) forms a bond with her sister Jiyoung (Baek Soo-hee) at this restaurant, Carino Hall.'),(5004571,'<Melting Me Softly(멜로가 체질)>In episode 9, Eun Jung (played by Won Jin Ah) walks down this street with her deceased boyfriend, Hong Dae, on their way to a restaurant.'),(5004572,'<Melting Melo(멜로가 체질)>Kimchi stew specialty restaurant where Yoon Ji-on and Jeon Sin-hwi are kicked out'),(5004573,'<Melting Me Softly(멜로가 체질)>A pork barbecue restaurant where Jeon Yeo-been and Son Seok-gu drink soju'),(5004575,'<Melting Me Softly(멜로가 체질)>Cafe that appeared in a past recollection scene in Jinju-Hwandong.'),(5004576,'<Melloga Chejil(멜로가 체질)> In episode 11, Son Beom-soo (Ahn Jae-hong) confesses his feelings to Im Jin-joo (Chun Woo-hee) here. And in episode 12, she suggests starting a date here and later kisses him.'),(5004577,'<Melting Me Softly(멜로가 체질)>In episode 8, Jin-ju (Chun Woo-hee) and Beom-su (Ahn Jae-hong) talk about people\'s emotions and complicated feelings while drink