een Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) and Lee Soo-ryun (Go Min-si), Kim Myung-hee (Kim Sae-ron) finds Hee-tae smoking in the garden.'),(5011017,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>This theme park is part of the Seoul neighborhood where Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) lives, along with several other places.'),(5011018,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>In episode 1, Kim Myung-hee (Go Min-shi) visits this church to meet with the priest (Yoo Soon-woong) in charge and inquire about the possibility of a university scholarship.'),(5011019,'<The Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>In episode 1, you will hear news of Yi Soo-ryeon\'s (Geum Sae-rok) arrest here. In episode 3, Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) and Myeong-hee meet here.'),(5011020,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>In episode 4, Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) and Kim Myeong-hee (Go Min-si) are seen walking down the alley near this house after returning from the orphanage.'),(5011021,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>In episode 2, Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) goes on a date with Kim Myung-hee (Go Min-si) who is still impersonating Lee Soo-ryeon (Geum Sae-rok) at this restaurant.'),(5011022,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>In episode 1, Hwang Heetae (played by Lee Do-hyun) meets his ex-girlfriend Yoojin (played by Go Eun-bin) at a cafe in Seoul. She asks him to marry her after their break-up. In episode 8, Lee Sooryun (played by Geum Saerok) moves to Seoul and visits this place alone. In a flashback scene in episode 10, Heetae and his friend Kim Kyungsoo (played by Kwon Young-chan) are also seen hanging out here.'),(5011023,'<Oh Waikiki(오월의 청춘)>In episode 8, Hwang Hee-tae (played by Lee Do-hyun) and Lee Su-ryeon (played by Go Min-si) take a walk on Deoksugung Stone Wall Path before Kim Myung-hee (played by Go Min-si) tells him the words she said to herself before leaving for Seoul. Afterwards, Su-ryeon tells Hee-tae, \"Let\'s break up here,\" and says, \"If a couple walks together on the Deoksugung Stone Wall Path, they will definitely break up.\"'),(5011024,'<Oh My Youth(오월의 청춘)>In episodes 1 and 2, Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) is waiting for a blind date at this restaurant. Kim Myeong-hee (Go Min-si) pretends to be Lee Soo-ryeon (Gum Saerok). In episode 4, Hee-tae meets Soo-ryeon (Gum Saerok) here and begs her to continue dating until the end of that month.'),(5011026,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>This is a major filming location for dramas.'),(5011027,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>In episode 6, Hwang Hee-tae (Lee Do-hyun) and Kim Myung-hee (Go Min-si) are seen playing at this amusement park with siblings Hwang Jung-tae (Choi Seung-hoon) and Kim Myung-soo (Choi Hyun-joon). They are joined by San Hui-tae as they ride the carousel and Viking ship.'),(5011028,'<Youth of May(오월의 청춘)>Hwang Hee-tae (played by Lee Do-hyun) and Lee Soo-ryun (played by Go Min-si), who are about to get engaged, come here to pick out an engagement gift led by their aunt (played by Kim Hyun)'),(5011029,'<Abyss Bridge Brothers(오작교 형제들)>Hwang Tae-bum (Ryu Soo-young) and Cha Soo-young (Choi Jung-yoon) appear as reporters working for IBC Broadcasting at Abyss Bridge Brothers.'),(5011030,'<Ojak Bridge Brothers(오작교 형제들)>In the final episode of episode 58, Hwang Tae-pil (Yeon Woo-jin) and Jung Yoon-suk (Jo Mi-ryeong) broke up and promised to meet again two years later.'),(5011031,'<Ojakgyo Brothers(오작교 형제들)>In episode 1, Hwang Tae-hee (Ju Won) follows the culprit into this street and arrests him in a situation where he must stop in front of the railroad tracks.'),(5011032,'<Ojakgyo Brothers(오작교 형제들)>In episode 1, Hwang Tae-hee (Joowon) chases the suspect across a pedestrian bridge connecting exit 3 and the station.'),(5011033,'<Ojakgyo Brothers(오작교 형제들)>In episode 1, Hwang Tae-hee (Ju Won) and his colleagues had a conversation on this street.'),(5011034,'<Ojakgyo Brothers(오작교 형제들)>The two protagonists of the drama hold their wedding ceremony in the Grand Ballroom of this convention center in episode 18.'),(5011035,'<Ojak Bridge Brothers(오작교 형제들)>The scene where Hwang Tae-sik (Jung Woong-in) is brought to his house in Episode 18.'),(5011036,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In the final episode 9, the scene where they come out to the airport to go to Los Angeles.'),(5011037,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 2, Seong Gi-hun (played by Lee Jung-jae) receives a call that his mother (played by Kim Young-ok) has been hospitalized and rushes to this hospital.'),(5011038,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>Seong Gi-hun (Lee Jung-jae) becomes involved in a high-stakes horse racing game in order to earn money to treat his daughter.'),(5011039,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>A fish store run by Sangwoo\'s mother'),(5011040,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episodes 1-2, Park Hye-jin plays Cho Sang-woo\'s mother who proudly displays a photo of her successful son at \'Sang-woo\'s Fish Shop,\' a fish store she operates in this market.'),(5011041,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>The place where Lee Jung-jae and Oh Yeong-su ate instant noodles and soju'),(5011042,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 2, Seong Gi-hun (Lee Jung-jae) visits his friend\'s (Lee Seo-hwan) bar to borrow money or work as a delivery driver to earn money for his mother\'s medical bills. His friend explains that he can\'t help him because he can barely pay rent, avoid eviction, and smoke cigarettes outside. Later, his friend is called back home by his wife and tells Gi-hun to follow, saying \"It\'s rude to smoke outside someone else\'s store.\"'),(5011043,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>\"Teacher, would you like to play a game with me?\" scene where the Squid Game officially starts.'),(5011044,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>After the game is canceled and participants return home, they realize that they missed an opportunity to improve their lives and accept a proposal to participate in the game again. In Round 2, Player 001, elderly man Oh Il-nam (Oh Young-soo) with a brain tumor, is escorted outside the hospital.'),(5011045,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>Head to the location where the game is being held from the entrance next to this building in Episode 1.'),(5011046,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 2, Jo Sang-woo (Park Hae-soo) and Ali Abdul (Tripathi Anupam) are released here after the game is abruptly terminated.'),(5011047,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 2, Sangwoo (played by Park Hae-soo) and Ali Abdul (played by Tripathi Anupam) return to Seoul and eat ramen at a Seven Eleven store.'),(5011048,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>A place where the Squid Game is interrupted by a vote and people part ways'),(5011049,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>Sang Ki-hun (Lee Jung-jae) urgently needs money as he celebrates his daughter\'s birthday in episode 1. He and his friend (Lee Se-hwan) go to a underground gambling company called \'Kora\' where Sang Ki-hun receives 4.5 million won. The situation quickly worsens after being caught by loan sharks.'),(5011050,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 2, Hwang Jun-ho (Wi Ha-Joon) comes to this dormitory to look for his brother, and discovers a Squid Game card in his room.'),(5011051,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 8 of Squid Game, the main character (Lee Byung-hun) and his followers chase after Seoul police and game infiltrator Hwang Jun-ho (Wi Ha-joon) to the edge of a cliff overlooking the western sea from the beach.'),(5011052,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>After the suspension of his game fixing scheme, gangster Jang Deok-su (played by Heo Sung-tae) meets an acquaintance outside this amusement park. In Episode 2, he proposes returning to the island with gang members to steal the prize money.'),(5011053,'<Squid Game(오징어게임)>In episode 2, Police officer Hwang Jun-ho (Wi Ha-joon) who suspects that Seong Gi-hun (Lee Jung-jae) can lead him to his missing brother, appears at this port following the van that transported him.'),(5011054,'<Okay Kwang Sisters(오케이 광자매)>As seen in episode 35, where Lee Kwang-shik (played by Jeon Hye-bin) tells him that his father has approved the marriage, Han Ye-seul (played by Kim Kyung-nam) lives in the rooftop room of this building.'),(5011055,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>In this place, Yong Tae-moo (Lee Tae-sung), Yong Tae-yong (Park Yoo-chun), and Park Ha (Han Ji-min) meet.'),(5011056,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>Filming of a Joseon Dynasty palace background took place here.'),(5011057,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>This is the path of Park Ha (Han Ji-min). While the boys chase after her, we see her working in Episode 7. In Episode 15, Park Ha and Yong Tae-yong (Park Yoo-chun) come back for a date.'),(5011058,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>In episode 15, Park Ha (Han Ji-min) and Yong Tae Yong (Park Yoochun) are here on a date and enjoying a fireworks show.'),(5011059,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>In the drama, Lee Gak (played by Park Yoochun) sees Hong Se-na (played by Jung Yoo-mi) advertising a lavish marriage proposal at this yacht club on a home shopping channel. After witnessing this, he realizes that his princess is about to marry someone else. In order to confront Se-na, Gak rushes to protect her from Yong Tae-moo (played by Lee Tae-sung), who is trying to harm her. However, Gak ends up falling from the yacht just like Yong Tae-yong (played by Park Yoochun) in the drama.'),(5011060,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>In episode 10, Yong Tae Yong (Park Yoochun) and Hong Se Na (Jung Yoo Mi) enjoy the night view at N Seoul Tower while Se Na continues with her schemes.'),(5011061,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>Scene where they take a break at the castle in episode 12'),(5011062,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)> She comes here after kissing in the 13th episode. She tells him she wants to live with him during the same period and when asked how long he plans to stay, he answers quietly.'),(5011063,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>In episode 2, Choi Woo-sik (Choi Woo-sik), Jung Seok-won (Yoo Yeong-sul), and Lee Gak (Lee Seung-gi) are depicted having thoughts about visiting the palace for the first time in the 21st century.'),(5011064,'<Rooftop Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>In episode 10, Yong Tae Yong (Park Yoochun) and Hong Se Na (Jung Yumi) take the cable car to N Seoul Tower to enjoy the night view.'),(5011065,'<Oktapbang Prince(옥탑방 왕세자)>The place where Prince Oktapbang, from the Joseo