he place where the main character, Jang Hee-bin (Kim Hye-soo), lives in the drama, and most of the scenes in the drama were filmed here.'),(5011874,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 16\'s final scene, Nam Chiwon (Choi Daniel) and Gwa Yun-yi (Baek Jin-hee) are taking a walk.'),(5011875,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>The lobby here is portrayed as the headquarters of \'YB Group\' in the drama.'),(5011876,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>Located against the backdrop of the YB Ad building, where most of the main cast members work. There is also a cafe owned by Kyungre (Jung Hye-in) in the lobby.'),(5011877,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 2, Nam Chiwon (played by Choi Daniel) comes to visit his late uncle to pay his respects. He also encounters Doo Bosang (played by Kim Chang Wan), who is a friend of his late uncle. This is where Seo Do-woo (played by Lee Sang-yoon) comes to find her in episodes 3 and 4. In episode 12, Kim Hye-won (played by Jang Hee-jin) comes to find her.'),(5011878,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>This place appears to be Wang Jung-ae\'s (played by Kang Hye-jung) house. In episode 2, characters Jo Yun-yi (played by Baek Jin-hee), Bona (played by Cha Joo-young), and Gyeong-rye (played by Jung Hye-in) visit the house.'),(5011879,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>While listening to a nagging about finding CEO Do\'s (Kim Chang-wan) house in episode 1, Nam Chi-won (Choi Daniel) asks to get off at the crosswalk and heads there.'),(5011880,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>The building that appears in the background when Choi Yoon Yi (Baek Jin Hee) calls a taxi in episode 1.'),(5011881,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>This is the place where Wang Jeong-ae (Kang Hye-jung) and her son Geon-woo (Jung Joon-won) lived. In episode 15, Hwang Bo-yool (Lee Won-geun) finishes his vacation and visits. Jeong-ae, who is upset that he is creating a scene at her house, gets up and leaves, with Yool following her. While they talk outside, the Hwang family\'s henchman secretly watches their conversation.'),(5011882,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>Episode 1 shows Jwa Yoon Yi (Baek Jin Hee) going on a date with his ex-girlfriend. At this park, her boyfriend Lee Kyung Joon (Seo Joon) received a phone call from his boss.'),(5011883,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 1, there is a brief appearance of Choi Sun-ah (Baek Jin-hee) on a date with her ex-boyfriend (Seo Joon).'),(5011884,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>They were together after Lacey (Baek Jin-hee) promised to hand over the key in episode 6. At first, the situation was a bit awkward for the team, but with him in the team, everyone was happy.'),(5011885,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 1, young YB director Hwang Bo-yul (Won Geun) commutes to work on his motorcycle on this bridge. In episode 8, Nam Chi-won (Daniel Choi) sits at one end of this bridge and realizes that Lawyer Jwa (Baek Jin-hee) may have shattered his trust.'),(5011886,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In the opening scene of the first episode, Jooyoon (played by Baek Jinhee) meets her ex-boyfriend and art curator, Kyeongjoon (played by Sung Jun). She explains her work inspired by the 1930 painting The Juggler by French artist Georges Rouault.'),(5011887,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>The place where Jwa Yoon-i (Baek Jin-hee) came to look for Nam Chi-won (Choi Daniel) on Lunar New Year\'s Day in episode 9.'),(5011888,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 8, Nam Chiwon (Choi Daniel) reaches out his hand to kiss Jwa Yoon Yi (Baek Jin Hee) at the top of this stairs.'),(5011889,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 8, Lawyer Jwa Yoon Yi (Baek Jin Hee) came here to find Nam Chi Won (Choi Daniel) who admires his deceased uncle.'),(5011890,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In this house lives Jwa Yoon Yi (played by Baek Jin-hee). In episode 3, Nam Chi-won\'s boss moves to the rooftop. It turns out that this place is the childhood home where he lived with his uncle after his family died in an accident. Chi-won decided to move here to confront and overcome the trauma of witnessing his uncle\'s death when the childhood home caught fire.'),(5011891,'<Jugglers(저글러스)>In episode 9, in a scene recalling the past, Wang Jeong-ae (Kang Hye-jung) passes by this photo studio. On that day, her husband Jun-pyo (Jeon Seok-ho) who is in the process of separating from her, tells her that he will leave for another family and reveals his plan to take out a life insurance policy for their son Geon-woo. Geon-woo (Jung Joon-won) is in college education. At the photo studio, as she stops in front of the window to look at a family photo of three people on display, her emotions start to bubble up and she yells angrily at his photo.'),(5011892,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>A restaurant featured in episode 5 where another dinner appointment is made. Kim Hae-kyung (played by Song Seung-heon) brings Woo Do-hee (played by Seo Ji-hye) here. After dinner, he gives her a penguin as a gift but suddenly has to leave. He assures her that he will be back soon. While waiting, she becomes increasingly intoxicated, nearly passing out just before his arrival, and begins lamenting about her past love.'),(5011893,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>In Kim Hae-kyung (played by Song Seung-heon)\'s \'Comfortable Mind Clinic,\' you can see Woo Do-hee (played by Seo Ji-hye) trying to meet him to scout him for the show she\'s producing in episode 4.'),(5011894,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>In \"La Fiesta,\" Kim Hae-kyung (played by Song Seung-heon) chases a patient on a motorcycle in the mall.'),(5011895,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>Featured in episode 7 as \'O & Cafe\'.'),(5011896,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>In episode 3, Kim Hae-kyung (played by Song Seung-heon) has a customer meeting at this restaurant where he appears as \'Moon Kang\'. He almost doesn\'t know that his ex-girlfriend Jin No-eul (played by Son Na-eun), whom he reserved under a pseudonym for the reunion, is here. At the same time, Woo Do-hee (played by Seo Ji-hye) arrives here to find Hae-kyung, but leaves without tracking him.'),(5011898,'<Let\'s have dinner together(저녁 같이 드실래요)>Woo Do-hee (Seo Ji-hye) takes Kim Hae-kyung (Song Seung-heon) to the food cart selling rice bowls \'Tiger Fist Rice\' and eats on the rooftop in episode 3. Shortly after, Jung Jae-hyuk (Lee Ji-hoon) also buys a bowl of rice from this food cart and goes up to the rooftop to eat. In episode 4, Do-hee and Hae-kyung pass by this place again to find each other.'),(5011899,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>In episode 1 of \"Udohee\", Udohee (played by Seo Ji-hye) arrives at this airport when she wants to surprise her boyfriend Youngdong (played by Kim Jung-hyun) on his birthday. In episode 1, Gae-hye-kyung (played by Song Seung-heon) takes Dohui from her boyfriend\'s cafe across the street to this airport.'),(5011900,'<Let\'s have dinner together(저녁 같이 드실래요)>In episode 2 (out of a total of 1), Woo Dohee (Seo Jihye) takes her boyfriend Youngdong (Kim Junghyun cameo) to this beach after finding out he cheated. Kim Haekyeong (Song Seungheon), who unknowingly planned to end his life after her, follows. As Dohee struggles to balance on the volcanic rock close to the sea, Haekyeong rushes in to save her. She bends down, falls into the sea, and eventually suffers a mild concussion.'),(5011901,'<Would you like to have dinner together?(저녁 같이 드실래요)>In episode 1 (total 1 episode), Woo Do-hee (Seo Ji-hye) talks about her favorite scene from the classic movie \'Breakfast at Tiffany\'s\' at the beginning.'),(5011902,'<Justice(저스티스)>The story is about a lawyer who defends the son of the National Tax Service, who has assaulted and sexually abused a classmate, and tries to get him acquitted of his crimes. In episode 2 (episode 1), he encounters Seo Yeon-a (Nana), who has become a prosecutor since their last trial. Song Woo-young (Son Hyun-joo), who went to the building with Tae-kyung, is also shown.'),(5011903,'<Justice(저스티스)>Hee Kyung (Choi Jin-hyuk) comes to evaluate a gangster who is ordered to be released in the 2nd episode (out of 1).'),(5011904,'<T