ood from a snack bar'),(5013254,'<Convenience Store Satbyeol(편의점 샛별이)>A gopchang restaurant where Ji Chang-wook meets his high school friend at Convenience Store Satbyeol'),(5013255,'<Convenience Store SaetByul(편의점 샛별이)>In Episode 1, Choi Hyun Jae (played by Ji Chang Wook) waits for the bus at this bus stop while on a date with his girlfriend. He goes to great lengths to safely raise a kitten he finds in a sewer, getting his clothes dirty in the process.'),(5013256,'<Convenience Store Saetbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)> In the first episode of \"The Spies Who Loved Me,\" the character played by Ji Chang-wook meets his girlfriend at this hotel.'),(5013257,'<Convenience Store Satbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)>In episode 12, Yoo Yeon-joo (Han Sun-hwa) receives a phone call while having dinner with Jo Seung-joon (Do Sang-woo) at this restaurant and quickly leaves.'),(5013258,'<Convenience Store Saetbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)>In the drama \'5회\', Yoo Yeon-joo (Han Sun-hwa) and Choi Dae-hyun (Ji Chang-wook) go on a drive, crossing this bridge after bringing her home.'),(5013259,'<Convenience Store Saebyeoli(편의점 샛별이)>In episode 6, Choimae Hyeon (Ji Chang-wook) parks his van at the end of Yeouido Bridge late at night and contemplates his relationship with Yoo Yeon-joo (Han Sun-hwa).'),(5013260,'<Convenience store Satbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)>Kim Yoo-jung and Ji Chang-wook\'s breakup Budae Jjigae restaurant at Convenience store Satbyeoli'),(5013261,'<Convenience Store Satbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)> In episodes 9 and 10, Yoo Yeon-joo (Han Sun-hwa) meets Joo Chang-wook (Ji Chang-wook) here and says goodbye. After that, she gets in Jo Seung-joon\'s (Do Sang-woo) car.'),(5013262,'<Convenience Store Saetbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)>The place where Ji Chang-wook and Han Sun-hwa watched a musical at Convenience Store Saetbyeoli'),(5013263,'<Convenience store Saetbyeol(편의점 샛별이)>You can see a scene where Yoo Yeon-joo (Han Sun-hwa) makes a surprise visit to the house where Choae-hyun (Ji Chang-wook) and his parents live in episode 8.'),(5013264,'<Convenience Store Saetbyeoli(편의점 샛별이)>In episode 12, Choi Yong-pil (Lee Byung-joon) is waiting for his wife Gong Boon-hee (Kim Sun-young) outside the neighborhood convenience store.'),(5013265,'<Convenience store Saetbyeol-i(편의점 샛별이)>Han Dalsik (Um Munsuk) and Hwanggeumbi (Seo Yehwa) wait at the intersection of this street in episode 11.'),(5013266,'<Weekday afternoon lovers(평일 오후 세시의 연인)>Son Ji-eun (Park Ha-sun) and Choi Soo-ah (Yeh Ji-won) make an appearance at this cafe in episode 16.'),(5013267,'<Weekdays at 3PM Lovers of the Three O\'clock(평일 오후 세시의 연인)>The exterior of this museum resembles that of Gallery White Block. It appears in episode 3 as a gallery operated by Kim Bitna (Yoo Seojin), a long-time friend of Lee Youngjae (Choi Byungmo).'),(5013268,'<Three O\'clock Date on a Weekday(평일 오후 세시의 연인)>The interior of this place appears as a gallery visited by Kim Bitna (played by Yoo Seojin), a long-time friend of Lee Youngjae (played by Choi Byeongmo), to discuss a business story.'),(5013269,'<Weekday Lover at 3 o\'clock(평일 오후 세시의 연인)>In the first episode, Choi Soo-ah (Ye Ji-won) dines with her family at this restaurant.'),(5013270,'<Forest(포레스트)>In episode 1 (out of 2 total), Jung Young-jae (played by Cho Bo-ah) is driving herself to the hospital she has been \'dispatched\' to, only to be led to this temple and find herself walking along the pine tree-lined path to the building.'),(5013271,'<Forest(포레스트)>In episodes 1-4, Kang San-hyuk (played by Park Hae-jin) works as a mergers and acquisitions director against the backdrop of the forest.'),(5013272,'<Forest(포레스트)>It appears to be Song Hye-won (Kim Tae-ri)\'s childhood home in the countryside.'),(5013273,'<Forest(포레스트)>In episode 27 (out of a total of 14 episodes), Park Hyeong-soo (Lee Si-hoon) came here to meet Taesung Group\'s Jo Kwang-pil (Kim Young-pil), and demanded the release of Jung Young-jae (Cho Bo-ah) from the police.'),(5013274,'<Forest(포레스트)>In episode 3, Kwon Hwayeon (played by Shin Ye-eun) and Lee Soo (played by Ong Seong-wu from Wanna One) walk down this street passing by a brunch cafe.'),(5013275,'<Forest(포레스트)>Kang San-hyuk\'s (played by Park Hae-jin) grandmother lived on this rooftop, and he returns to this place and his memories.'),(5013276,'<Pongdang Pongdang LOVE(퐁당퐁당 LOVE)>This park is the palace of Lee Do (Yoon Doo-joon), where Jang Danbi (Kim Seul-gi) time travels.'),(5013277,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In the final episode of the 20th round, Heo Jun-jae (Lee Min-ho) and Shim Cheong (Jun Ji-hyun) happily drive along this winding road overlooking the blue sea.'),(5013278,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 20, this beach cafe appears as the happy home where Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho) and Shim Cheong (Jun Ji-hyun) live.'),(5013279,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Heo Junjae (Lee Minho) takes Simcheong (Jun Jihyun) to the place where it snows the most. He teaches her how to ski, but before he can finish explaining how to brake, she zooms down the slope. He grabs her and they both tumble in the snow. After Junjae finally stops her, he asks her to pronounce a word. When she repeats \"I love you,\" it almost sounds like a confession when he asks her to say it again. But in reality, he just wants to remember her voice and confirm that it is hers.'),(5013280,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>The place where Jun Jae and Cheong Ah went on a skiing date.'),(5013282,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>This is where appeared as a beach church in episode 2 of Spain in the drama series. Here, Heo Jun-jae (played by Lee Min-ho) and Shim Cheong (played by Jun Ji-hyun) are chased by their colleague scam artist \'Thomas Missionary\' (played by Ahn Jae-hong) and seek refuge and support. After spending a night, Thomas and Jun-jae share the money they have collected as fake pastors and leave the next morning.'),(5013283,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>This is where the broker from Episode 9 of the new TV series meets some wealthy ladies to give investment advice.'),(5013284,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>A place where the beauty and harmony of the Joseon Dynasty are reunited'),(5013285,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Appears as the Spanish shopping mall visited by Shim Cheong (played by Jun Ji-hyun) and Heo Joon-jae (played by Lee Min-ho) in episode 1.'),(5013286,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Place where Choi and Junjae from the Joseon Dynasty stayed'),(5013287,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>The place where the legend of Danryeong, who helps the blue and chases away the blue, is engraved.'),(5013288,'<The Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 1, Heo Jun-jae (Lee Min-ho) bewitches a woman with magic at a bar.'),(5013289,'<The Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Heo Jun-jae (Lee Min-ho) sheds tears as he gets off the elevator in episode 3 and asks his team members who are waiting for him to sue him.'),(5013290,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>This is where Shim Cheong (played by Jun Ji-hyun) and Heo Joon-jae (played by Lee Min-ho) go on a date in episode 14. Joon-jae promises to always live happily with Shim Cheong, but when he suddenly dies, he asks her to find a new partner, ending their date abruptly. She can only love one person for a lifetime, which is something she cannot do as a mermaid.'),(5013291,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>This is also the office where the trio of scammers Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho), Jo Nam-doo (Lee Hee-joon), and Tae-oh (Shin Won-ho) disguise themselves as elevator operators to welcome the \'customers\' couple in episode 1.'),(5013292,'<Legend of Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 3, Shim Cheong (Jeon Ji-hyun) meets Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho) to swim in the aquarium.'),(5013293,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 7, hungry Shim Cheong (played by Gianna Jun) searches for fish here. Meanwhile, she meets her fellow mermaid Joo Jung-hoon (played by Cho Jung-seok).'),(5013294,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 4, Shim Chung (Jun Ji-hyun) followed Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho) here. He saved her from a con artist, they watched a fire festival together, and he hesitated before taking her to his home.'),(5013295,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>The place where Cheong and Junjae promised to meet on the first snowfall'),(5013296,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 5, a scene was depicted where Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho) drives on the road east of Namsan Library towards Namsan Tower on the first snowy day.'),(5013297,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 8, Heo Jun-jae (Lee Min-ho) visits to meet his own self (Damyung) with Shim Cheong (Jun Ji-hyun).'),(5013298,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Heo Jun-jae (Lee Min-ho) spent his childhood here until his parents divorced. This is where his father Heo Il-joong (Choi Jung-woo) and stepmother Kang Seo-hee (Hwang Shin-hye), and stepbrother Heo Chi-hyun (Lee Ji-hoon) live. It is also the place where his father was murdered.'),(5013299,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Cha Si-ah (Shin Hye-sun) appears as her workplace. In episodes 9 and 10, she brings Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho) and shows them a portrait of Dam-ryeong, their most recent discovery. As they enter the storage room, Joon-jae realizes that Dam-ryeong resembles himself.'),(5013300,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>This is another part of Heo Joon-jae\'s (Lee Min-ho) house where he and everyone else live. The rooftop, balcony, and living room scenes were filmed here.'),(5013301,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 11, the funeral of Heo Il-joong (Choi Jung-woo), the father of Heo Joon-jae (Lee Min-ho), takes place at the CKU Hospital VVIP Hall.'),(5013302,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episodes 15 and 16, Jun Jae (Lee Min Ho) meets his mother again.'),(5013303,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>This place is where the con artist Heo Jun-jae (Lee Min-ho) cons and joins forces with his two criminal partners, Jo Nam-doo (Lee Hee-joon) and Tae-oh (Shin Won-ho), in Episode 1. Nam-doo refers to Jun-jae as a better version of a Harry Potter con artist.'),(5013304,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>The tower appears as the background in episode 1.'),(5013305,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 3, she is welcomed by a group of ahjummas who have come here to witness the \"Miracle of Moses,\" likened to the parting of the sea.'),(5013306,'<Legends of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>In episode 4, Shim Cheong (played by Jun Ji-hyun) comes here to meet Dam Ryung (played by Lee Min-ho) and gets surrounded by the swordsmen of the nobleman. She is eventually rescued by Dam Ryung in episode 5. He later presents her with a pine tree flower symbolizing \"memories.\"'),(5013307,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>A place where modern art and tradition meet'),(5013308,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Came to go on a date with a flight attendant met on a flight to Spain in episode 1.'),(5013309,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>A place where modern fruit seller Junde gets chased by gangsters.'),(5013310,'<Legend of the Blue Sea(푸른 바다의 전설)>Background where Dam-ryeong appears in episode 1'),(5013311,'<Dignified Lady(품위있는 그녀)>In episode 20, Kim Hyo-joo (Lee Hee-jin) stays at the penthouse.'),(5013312,'<Scenery(풍경)>In Episode 1, Daniel (B1A4\'s Jung Jinyoung) passes by this mansion while exploring Seoul and gives a gift to a girl who lost her balloon.'),(5013313,'<Scenery(풍경)>In the first episode, Yoo Jin (Mina) represents the company at a book fair held in this park.'),(5013314,'<Heard through rumors(풍문으로 들었소)>In episode 30, Su (Jeong Yujin) and her sister-in-law Jeong (Le Jun) leave, and Han (Go A-sung) and Seo (Go A-sung) come to say goodbye.'),(5013315,'<Balloon Gum(풍선껌)>In episode 6, Park Li-hwan (Lee Do-wook) and Kim Haeng-a (Jeong Ryeo-won) came to this beach and had a date.'),(5013316,'<Bubble Gum(풍선껌)>This is where there is a tree honoring Kim Haeng-ah\'s (Jung Ryeo-won) father. She visits here with Park Ri-hwan (Lee Dong-wook) in epi